      "writtenOn": "2024-12-26T18:09:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yep. `CTypeRef` (taken by `MakeMetal` on line 64) is really just `const void*`. So you can have one in C++ code. And the C++ wrappers for Metal provided by Apple let you just pass `MTL::Texture*`. The `MTL::` classes are really just interfaces around underlying Obj-C types that have been pointer-casted to the equivalent C++ wrapper type. So a `MTL::Texture*` is actually a `id\u003cMTLTexture\u003e` and a therefore a valid `CTypeRef`.",
      "parentUuid": "ff2b6a11_afc4846d",
