      "writtenOn": "2024-12-26T18:33:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The middle one, absolutely. It\u0027s the reason I\u0027m making the change. I see no reason to exclude the other two, though. By forward declaring them we allow a `MtlTextureInfo` that is created in some Objective-C++ code (that *can* see the definition of `MtlTextureInfo`) to pass by pointer or reference to C++ only code that just sees the forward declarations of `MtlTextureInfo` and the first `MakeMetal` on line 63. That C++ code can then pass the `MetalTextureInfo` by reference to the Objective-C++ implementation of `MakeMetal` in Skia.",
      "parentUuid": "bec37ef9_8ce25cc6",
